  "final_message": "Incident center is built and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask + SQLite at `./data/incident-center.db` (WAL, auto-created on startup). Token-based Bearer auth stored in DB so sessions survive restarts; PBKDF2 password hashing. All incident endpoints per spec: paged list (`severity`/`status`/`open`/`q`/`page`/`page_size`, newest opened first), create in `investigating`, PATCH that only touches given fields, auto-appends a `status_change` event on status change, sets/clears `resolved_at`, and bumps `reopen_count` on reopen. `sla_due_at` = `opened_at` + 60/240/1440/4320 min per severity; `sla_breached` = resolved past target or still open past it. `GET /api/public/stats` is unauthenticated; validation errors return 400 with a `details` field map. 401/404/405 under `/api` return JSON; SPA fallback serves `frontend/dist`.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React 19 + TS + Vite 8 + Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`, only CSS file is `src/index.css`), react-router with pages: login/register, public overview (per-severity open counts + breached count), incident list (filters, open-only switch, debounced search, paging, breach flags), incident detail (fields, status buttons, timeline, post-event form), and open-incident form that renders the API's validation messages. Token kept in localStorage; stale tokens auto-redirect to sign-in. `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm ci && npm run build` works (Docker path validated).\n\nTested against a live gunicorn instance on :8000 \u2014 full curl suite passed; workspace `data/` and `__pycache__` cleaned up.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
  "max_turns_hit": false,
